    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "therapy doesn't change the fact that the athlete is gone. you can't therapist your way back into having a purpose. it's like being a spectator to your own life. i spend all day just waiting for the day to be over, and even then, i just wake up as this same empty thing again. it's just exhausting to keep performing \"life\" when there's nothing left inside to drive it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
